.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MK.FRAMEWORK.MK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk.framework.mk
.Nd framework role: builds its modules in dependency order
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fd .include <mk.framework.mk>
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A framework is a directory of modules with public headers in
.Pa include/ .
Any immediate subdirectory named
.Pa *.m
is a module and
.Pa *.tst
a test module; they are found without being listed, and built in the order
their
.Va LIBS
imply.
.Ss Variables
.Bl -tag -width "PUBLIC_HEADERS_SYSTEM"
.It Va PREREQS
Required, even empty.
The frameworks whose public headers and libraries this one may use, in order.
A framework is recognised by setting it.
.It Va PUBLIC_HEADERS_SYSTEM
.Cm yes :
consumers get this framework's headers with
.Fl isystem
instead of
.Fl I ,
for a framework wrapping third-party code.
.It Va PLATFORMS , Va TOOLCHAINS , Va REASON. Ns Ar entry
Where the whole framework is built; see
.Xr mk.constraints.mk 5 .
.It Va FW
With
.Cm add-prereq :
the framework to add.
.It Va TEST
With
.Cm test :
only the modules declaring this test.
.El
.Ss Targets
.Bl -tag -width "add-prereq"
.It Cm all
Build every module and copy its output up.
This is the default.
.It Cm copy-up
Build, then copy this framework's output to the workspace.
.It Cm test
Run every module's tests; see
.Xr mk.test.mk 5 .
.It Cm docs
Document this framework; see
.Xr mk.docs.mk 5 .
.It Cm clean
Remove this framework's and its modules' output for the current key.
.It Cm add-prereq
Append
.Va FW
to
.Va PREREQS
in the makefile.
It edits text only and looks nothing up.
.It Cm help
Print the current selection and the usual variables.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "build/KEY/runs/RUN_ID/build.log"
.It Pa include/
public headers
.It Pa build/ Ns Ar KEY Ns Pa /{bin,lib,include,share}/
what the modules copied up
.It Pa build/ Ns Ar KEY Ns Pa /runs/ Ns Ar RUN_ID Ns Pa /build.log
this run's output; each module has its own
.It Pa .gen-mod-order.mk
the module order, generated
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Non-zero if any module failed, even when the run went on past it.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
PREREQS=System Math
PUBLIC_HEADERS_SYSTEM=yes
\&.include <mk.framework.mk>
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It PREREQS= must be defined (even if empty) in a framework makefile
Set
.Va PREREQS ,
to nothing if the framework has no prerequisites.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bmake-it 7 ,
.Xr mk.constraints.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.lib.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.prog.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.tst.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.workspace.mk 5
